You are merging per-chunk partial lecture notes into ONE coherent hierarchical summary of the
whole lecture.

Lecture title: {{ lecture_title }}
Language: {{ language }}. Write the final summary in {{ language }}.

Rules:
- Merge duplicate or overlapping sections and highlights into single entries; preserve every
  distinct point mentioned in the partials.
- For each merged section, keep the EARLIEST `timestamp_seconds` observed across the partials
  that contributed to it.
- Do NOT add facts that are absent from the partials. This is a merge, not an expansion.
- Reorder sections chronologically by `timestamp_seconds` when the ordering across partials
  is ambiguous.
- Respect the target schema exactly; every field is required unless it is a list, which may be empty.
- Return VALID JSON ONLY. No Markdown, no commentary, no prose outside the JSON.

Target schema (`SummaryDocument`):
{
  "title": string,                       // reuse or lightly refine the lecture title
  "language": "{{ language }}",
  "sections": [
    {
      "heading": string,
      "timestamp_seconds": number,
      "bullets": [string, ...],
      "highlights": [
        {
          "kind": "definition" | "formula" | "example" | "key_point",
          "text": string,
          "timestamp_seconds": number
        }
      ],
      "subsections": [ /* same shape as a section, may be empty */ ]
    }
  ]
}

